# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CLIENT-SIDE — compiled into the public bundle. Public forever, to everyone.
#
# Only the two variables below may carry a VITE_ prefix. The anon key is safe
# here because row-level security, not key secrecy, protects the data behind it.
# Leave both blank to run local-only: scans still work, sign-in and history are
# hidden.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SERVER-SIDE — never add a VITE_ prefix to anything below this line.
#
# These belong in Supabase Edge Function secrets, not in this file and not in
# the bundle:
#
#   supabase secrets set ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=...
#   supabase secrets set STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=...
#
# The service_role key bypasses RLS entirely — it grants full read and write on
# every row of every table. It has no legitimate use in this repository at all;
# it is listed here only so its name is recognisable when you see it elsewhere.
#
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY   (never needed here)
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY           (Phase 2 — Claims module, Edge Function only)
#   STRIPE_SECRET_KEY           (later — billing)
#
# `checkClientEnv` refuses to start the app if any of these appear with a VITE_
# prefix, by name or by value shape. `npm run verify` additionally scans the
# built bundle. Both are in src/lib/env.ts.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
